<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila mauritiana Turing wavelength at 1.6 µm (Pass 1, free branch) (Drosophila mauritiana)",
        "Drosophila mauritiana Turing wavelength at 1.6 µm (Pass 1, free branch) faithfully reproduces Drosophila mauritiana morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila mauritiana specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila mauritiana" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That the free spot field is a photograph of the genital arch.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery sepia spiral is a SEM.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor comparison uses the recorded kikkawai cellular wavelength 93.41 µm, not that slot's parameters.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a = 0.10, b = 0.90, D_v/D_u = 9.875, γ chosen so k_max sits on 1.637 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Glassford et al. 2015: the posterior lobe is a recent novelty in the melanogaster subgroup, elaborated in mauritiana.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: that wavenumber is the intrinsic pre-pattern wavelength and it moves with the diffusivity ratio.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: two morphogens can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 1.637 µm target is this slot's assigned detail scale. Gompel 2005 and Glassford 2015 do not report that number." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila mauritiana (Mauritius Endemic Fruit Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_free_field.gif; organism: Drosophila mauritiana; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: two morphogens can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Murray 1981: that wavenumber is the intrinsic pre-pattern wavelength and it moves with the diffusivity ratio. | Glassford et al. 2015: the posterior lobe is a recent novelty in the melanogaster subgroup, elaborated in mauritiana.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a = 0.10, b = 0.90, D_v/D_u = 9.875, γ chosen so k_max sits on 1.637 µm. | Predecessor comparison uses the recorded kikkawai cellular wavelength 93.41 µm, not that slot's parameters.; transfer_boundary: The 1.637 µm target is this slot's assigned detail scale. Gompel 2005 and Glassford 2015 do not report that number.; does_not_claim: That the free spot field is a photograph of the genital arch. | That the gallery sepia spiral is a SEM.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2015.08.005>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03235>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://codex.flywire.ai/>,
        <https://flybase.org/>,
        <https://flycellatlas.org/>,
        <https://insitu.fruitfly.org/>,
        <https://www.virtualflybrain.org/> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Sophophora melanogaster Subgroup Radiation (0–12 Ma)" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
